### Insertion Before the Value X in a Linked List

**Problem:** Given the head of a singly linked list and two integers `X` and `val`, insert a new node with value `val` before the node containing value `X` and return the head of the modified linked list.

**Approach:**

- Check if the linked list is empty (`head == null`). If so, return `head`.
- If the head node contains the value `X`, insert the new node before the head by setting `newNode.next = head` and return the new node as the updated head.
- Otherwise, create a new node with the given value `val`.
- Initialize a temporary pointer with the head node.
- Traverse the linked list until the next node contains the value `X` or the end of the list is reached.
- If the value `X` is found, connect the new node to the target node (`newNode.next = temp.next`).
- Update the previous node's next reference to the new node (`temp.next = newNode`).
- If the value `X` is not present, leave the linked list unchanged.
- Return the updated head.

**Time Complexity:** O(n) – In the worst case, the entire linked list is traversed to find the node containing value X.

**Space Complexity:** O(1) – Only one new node and a temporary pointer are used.

**Concepts Used:**
- Singly Linked List
- Node Insertion
- Insertion Before a Given Value
- Head Pointer
- Temporary Pointer
- Searching
- Pointer Manipulation
- Node Linking
- Null Checking

###Solution

/*
Definition of singly Linked List:
class ListNode{
    public int data;
    public ListNode next;
    ListNode() { data = 0; next = null; }
    ListNode(int x) { data = x; next = null; }
    ListNode(int x, ListNode next) { data = x; this.next = next; }
}
*/

class Solution {
    public ListNode insertBeforeX(ListNode head, int X, int val) {
        // If the list is empty, nothing can be inserted before X
        if (head == null) {
            return null;
        }
        
        // If X is at the head, insert the new node at the very beginning
        if (head.data == X) {
            return new ListNode(val, head);
        }
        
        // Traverse the list to find the node right before the node with value X
        ListNode current = head;
        while (current.next != null) {
            if (current.next.data == X) {
                ListNode newNode = new ListNode(val, current.next);
                current.next = newNode;
                break; // Stop after inserting before the first occurrence of X
            }
            current = current.next;
        }
        
        return head;
    }
}

